          "at": "2026-07-20T08:24:03.064476+00:00",
          "body": "**Audit correction (2026-07-20).** The advertised RD-N steps A/B/C are not sufficient. On a pinned chart `B = \u0393(V)`, `range (chartReadMap)` is only an `R`-submodule `P`; RD-N concerns the genuine ideal `J = B \u00b7 P`. The landed flatness is flatness of `B/P` as an `R`-module and does not imply purity after quotienting by the chosen equation.\n\nA guard example is `R = k[\u03b5]/(\u03b5\u00b2)`, `B = R[t]`, `P = R\u00b7t + R\u00b7(t\u00b2+\u03b5)`, `s=t`: `B/P` is `R`-free and the reduced fibre is locally generated by `t`, but the ideal image `J/(t) = (\u03b5)` has nonzero residue fibre at `(\u03b5,t)`. Thus fibre achiever divisibility cannot by itself prove the sharp `\u03ba(z)` tensor vanishes.\n\nThe corrected critical path is to use the **second Grassmannian window** to prove a relative persistence/purity theorem (first establish `K_prime = H_s \u00b7 K` from P-fib in every residue field and finite-module Nakayama), then deduce ideal-level local generation/RD-N. Landed audit infrastructure: `DivSchemeFibrePoint.lean` (`abac842cc`), sharp `\u03ba(z)` consumer (`ca7c437d4`), genuine `chartReadIdeal` and its equality with `chartColengthModule` (`e0a718b0c`), and the generic fibre-surjectivity/Nakayama theorem (`b67d9b09`, `77e1f3bd`). Do not reuse the old chart-flat inference."
