      "body": "Blueprint Lean-name resolver does not honor the _root_. escape (dashboard blind spot)\n\nFound during the m33 blueprint pass (commit 3900cfd4e). A blueprint node whose \\lean{} names a declaration written as '_root_.foo' inside an enclosing 'namespace Bar' shows lean_status: empty in the DAG JSON, even though the decl exists and is kernel-green \u2014 the resolver strips or mis-resolves the _root_. escape. Concrete instance: lem:ringKrullDim_quotient_eq_coheight \u2192 ringKrullDim_quotient_eq_coheight (Milne33CMEquidim.lean:283, a '_root_.'-escaped lemma inside namespace RingTheory). The \\lean name is the correct grep-verified root name; writing anything else would be factually wrong, so this is a resolver/tooling fix, not a blueprint-source fix. Class of bug: affects every '_root_.'-escaped decl noded anywhere in the project. Next action: teach the blueprint Lean-name resolver (leandag/hgraph sync) to normalize the _root_. prefix before matching against declaration names; low priority (dashboard cosmetic, does not affect kernel verification).",
