      "body": "ADJUDICATION \u2014 the DAT-D functor pin's global certificate is WRONG: currently-pinned divFunctor is representable by NO scheme; the locally-certified repair is frozen (spec-dd-2 Addendum 2). DD-R lane: DDR-9 must restate divRep against DivFamZar. Supersedes the 'certificate brick' plan inside I-0209 (the Z-clopen PRINCIPLE there stays valid \u2014 it is exactly what powers this counterexample).\n\nTHE COUNTEREXAMPLE (campaign-central): R = \u0393(C minus a point off the 0/infinity fibers); d = the DIAGONAL section of C_R (the campaign's own graph-divisor, AJCR.picard.degree.graph), a degree-1 relative effective divisor. Every piece P inside one pinned chart has Z-trace = Delta(U_P) with U_P a PROPER open of the CONNECTED Spec R, and (c1) forces U_P clopen, hence empty \u2014 NO globally certified adaptation of d exists, while d IS certifiable over each member of a small basic-open cover of Spec R (the diagonal locally stays in one chart). Therefore: (1) certified families over a base cover can glue to a non-certifiable family \u2014 the S5 conditional keystone's hcert is UNSATISFIABLE in general and the W-idempotent brick cannot fix it (here W = R, no idempotents); (2) DivFam (globally certified) satisfies separation but NOT gluing \u2014 it is not a Zariski sheaf, so no scheme represents the pinned divFunctor, and DDR-9's divRep as currently stated is unprovable. Independently, the divRep forward map 'pull the universal family' is ill-defined for test maps not landing in one chart member \u2014 same phenomenon from the other side.\n\nTHE REPAIR (faithful to Kleiman df:red/lm:ctn, where divisor-flatness is Zariski-LOCAL on the base): the functor value is the LOCALLY-certified quotient DivFamZar n R := {d : LocalEquations // IsLocallyCertified n d}/DivEq, with IsLocallyCertified = exists finite span-top (g : Fin m -> R) and per-i a CertifiedDivisorFamily over Localization.Away (g i) whose eqns are DivEq to the pulled d (hreg free along open immersions \u2014 S5 Kit). CertifiedDivisorFamily/DivFam remain THE building block; over a field the two notions agree (trivial cover), so ALL DD-4 (epsilon/windows/mono), DD-1c field dictionary, DAT-B field-level material is UNAFFECTED. With the repair the pinned keystone DivFamZar.exists_glue_of_away_compat becomes TRUE with already-landed ingredients (S5 awayGluedEquations + chart restrictions + composite covers + total mapAlg). IMPACT ROWS: DD-R/DDR-9 \u2014 restate divRep homEquiv against the DivFamZar vehicle (the universal family pulls back to a LOCALLY certified family along arbitrary test maps: maps into the chart atlas are local \u2014 this is exactly why the repair also FIXES the forward map); DDR-6/8 chart-local work unaffected; DD-4 unaffected; DAT-C consumes chart-level data unaffected. Implementation: S5b (DivFamZar + keystone) in flight in this lane; S6 (divFunctor packaging) follows on DivFamZar. Vocabulary pins added: IsLocallyCertified, DivFamZar, DivFam.toZar, DivFamZar.mapAlg, DivFamZar.picClass, DivFamZar.eq_of_away_eq, DivFamZar.exists_glue_of_away_compat.",
