      "body": "THE Z-CLOPEN CERTIFICATE PRINCIPLE (DD-1/DD-2 lanes, 2026-07-17 \u2014 three independent sightings in one day; treat as a standing design constraint for every DAT-D brick).\n\nA DivisorAdaptation piece carries an R-finite-projective colength \u2014 clause (c1) of IsCertified \u2014 IFF the piece's trace on the divisor scheme Z = V(D) (finite flat over Spec R) is CLOPEN in Z. Any construction that slices Z along the base (basic-open refinement of pieces, denominator-cleared pieces from a localization cover, Z-blind extraction) produces section rings like R_u that are NOT finite over R, and the certificate is unrecoverable \u2014 the localization-span descent lemmas' hypotheses are FALSE, not merely hard. Canonical counterexample: R = k[u], zero-section divisor, cleared piece D(u-tilde): colength = R_u.\n\nConsequences adjudicated today: (1) the DD-1 pt-transport seam could NOT be fixed by extraction + certificate transport (certificates are not refinement-stable) \u2014 fixed instead by the S1 carrier surgery (point-free eqn_rel, total mapAlg, commit 19c79359); (2) DD-2 S5's glued adaptation could NOT take its certificate from denominator-cleared pieces (spec-dd-2 section-5 route corrected in the addendum) \u2014 the gluing keystone landed CONDITIONAL on hcert (exists_glue_of_away_compat_of_certifiedRep, commit 1758fad90).\n\nTHE MISSING BRICK (next in the DD-2 lane; coordinate with DD-R before speccing \u2014 same substrate as DDR-4's engine bridge, spec-dd-r section-7 risk 1): W-as-algebra extraction \u2014 the glued colength W(d) of a certified family is a finite projective R-ALGEBRA (= Gamma(Z)); its canonical idempotents (glued via the module-localization sheaf sequence over the away cover) split Z into packets; CRT-separated chart generators give packet-swallowing basic-open pieces whose traces are clopen; that adaptation carries the certificate and discharges hcert, upgrading the conditional keystone to the pinned DivFam.exists_glue_of_away_compat. Only then can S6 deliver divFunctor at full strength for DDR-9.",
